# Source is always diffable. Without this, git sniffs content and will silently
# treat a file as binary if it finds a NUL in the first 8k — which src/skills.ts
# did, because it used raw NUL bytes as a composite-key separator. The effect was
# that `git diff` and GitHub review both rendered "Binary files differ" for the
# file holding the plugin trust gate: changes to the highest-risk code in the
# repo were invisible to review. The bytes are now written as \0 escapes, and
# this makes the guarantee explicit rather than dependent on content sniffing.
*.ts   text diff
*.js   text diff
*.json text diff
*.md   text diff
*.yml  text diff
